.TH LS.LUA 1 "October 2026" "ls.lua 0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ls.lua \- list directory contents, written in Lua
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ls.lua
[\fB\-a1l\fR] [\fIDIR\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ls.lua
lists the entries of each \fIDIR\fR (default: the current directory),
sorted by byte value. Names starting with a dot are hidden unless
\fB\-a\fR is given. On a terminal, directories are blue, symlinks cyan
and executables green.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-a
Do not hide entries starting with a dot.
.TP
.B \-l
Long format: mode, links, owner, group, size, mtime, name.
.TP
.B \-1
One entry per line.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 2 if a directory could not be read or an option is invalid.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ls (1),
.BR readdir (3),
.BR stat (2)
